<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-23T20:01:12Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Russia's attacks on Ukraine's capital, Kyiv, are intensifying. DW asked people on the ground what life is like</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6069ff23f283c767f688fa3774236f13a03d5aa0a9d11160eb4caafca269b8c</id><updated>2026-10-23T20:00:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T19:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-attacks-on-ukraine-s-capital-kyiv-are-intensifying-dw-asked-people-on-the-ground-what-life-/a-79741090--9d6ca1b7b337.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-attacks-on-ukraine-s-capital-kyiv-are-intensifying-dw-asked-people-on-the-ground-what-life-is-like/a-79741090?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's attacks on the Ukrainian capital are hitting harder and more frequently, making 2026 one of the long war's bloodiest years for Kyiv. DW asked people on the ground what life is like.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Jordan: Karak church shooting leaves 7 dead, dozens injured</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28d83f4b35487cca3cdd916597beb082b5f33bb0f6fdeb355a9568fee40b2b64</id><updated>2026-10-23T20:00:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T18:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jordan-karak-church-shooting-leaves-7-dead-dozens-injured/a-79743535--fb132a258471.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jordan-karak-church-shooting-leaves-7-dead-dozens-injured/a-79743535?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A shooting at a Greek Orthodox church in southern Jordan happened during a funeral, according to authorities. Two unidentified men opened fire on the procession, with Jordan's king vowing "the harshest retaliation."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia, Ukraine agree to US-brokered, 1 city ceasefire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e68967da1a8b70603330df4f8decde4f75a5cec0f83d7943a0956ceb2a9f00bd</id><updated>2026-10-23T20:00:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T18:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-ukraine-agree-to-us-brokered-1-city-ceasefire/a-79746723--d5b21a176374.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-ukraine-agree-to-us-brokered-1-city-ceasefire/a-79746723?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Ukrainian city of Oleshky, occupied by Russia and on the frontline, faces a humanitarian crisis. The localized truce comes as Ukrainian President Zelenskyy said negotiators would meet for wider talks next month.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Afghan women could lose one of their last paths to a higher education</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:578b379d0c2b5cd57abfc19d92fa2988727a506abd59684ada98f5495db7db38</id><updated>2026-10-23T20:01:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afghan-women-could-lose-one-of-their-last-paths-to-a-higher-education/a-79745173--2a76364e2679.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afghan-women-could-lose-one-of-their-last-paths-to-a-higher-education/a-79745173?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US has defunded one of the last universities giving Afghan women the chance to receive an education after the Taliban takeover in 2021. DW spoke with a student who says she's lost hope of ever earning a degree.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Romania blames Russia for ship attack in the Black Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1fb9d7e5bcdd72111d5e8f775a6f8700b501635a2fbf8161dc5d5f079023993d</id><updated>2026-10-23T20:01:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/romania-blames-russia-for-ship-attack-in-the-black-sea/a-79743425--1bf4cd10b7ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/romania-blames-russia-for-ship-attack-in-the-black-sea/a-79743425?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian strikes against ships attempting to export Ukrainian grain and cargo through the western Black Sea have sharply increased this month.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine tries to shut Moscow's airports with drone strikes on Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08561186b336123810a2234c3d6dcf35bc12815aad6f3ae06787975fbfbf5225</id><updated>2026-10-23T20:01:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-tries-to-shut-moscow-s-airports-with-drone-strikes-on-russia/a-79737469--16f9cb7db516.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-tries-to-shut-moscow-s-airports-with-drone-strikes-on-russia/a-79737469?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Repeated Ukrainian drone attacks are increasingly disrupting operations at Moscow's airports. The pounding is part of Ukraine's plan to shut down Russia's airpace.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Many feared trapped under collapsed building in Nairobi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74eda5273ee52652da55ccb528d9634eec7a7663825d377fc43319233a7bc34f</id><updated>2026-10-23T20:01:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/many-feared-trapped-under-collapsed-building-in-nairobi/a-79744598--3192a74714c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/many-feared-trapped-under-collapsed-building-in-nairobi/a-79744598?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">People are feared to be trapped after a large, unfinished building in Nairobi collapsed during construction. Rescue operations have proven complicated as police fired tear gas to disperse looters.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Japan-Russia ties erode as journalist sits in Moscow jail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21d35a5914fe55fa5d9daf4a7993827038c96cfd5bd3316b2dc982a1f2c25b2f</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T12:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-russia-ties-erode-as-journalist-sits-in-moscow-jail/a-79742995--090b57f76cf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-russia-ties-erode-as-journalist-sits-in-moscow-jail/a-79742995?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Japan is demanding access to a journalist who was arrested by Russian security services. The Kremlin claims that Japan is using journalists as spies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda says it has no active Ebola cases, but infections in Kenya and Nigeria are prompting fresh scrutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85b05148fe9d66fcec28e83974135e2866e5a53849f839c31ffd863a6644152a</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T12:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-says-it-has-no-active-ebola-cases-but-infections-in-kenya-and-nigeria-are-prompting-fresh-scr/a-79741580--819bf739b307.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-says-it-has-no-active-ebola-cases-but-infections-in-kenya-and-nigeria-are-prompting-fresh-scrutiny/a-79741580?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Health officials are investigating whether Ebola patients in Kenya and Nigeria crossed paths at Uganda's main airport as conflicting accounts cloud the source of one infection.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia: Hope, tension and apprehension as voters prepare to elect new parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:600634f5f9dbbbc215efcd7cb7b13f92958df24b23d8c0ba221ad5d19a32b15b</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-hope-tension-and-apprehension-as-voters-prepare-to-elect-new-parliament/a-79738102--35e507b36c9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-hope-tension-and-apprehension-as-voters-prepare-to-elect-new-parliament/a-79738102?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After two years of protests, Serbia faces a pivotal election on Sunday, with a student-led challenge to Aleksandar Vucic's lengthy rule. Allegations of electoral irregularities and fears of a post-election crisis abound.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>France: 1 killed, 4 wounded after shooting near Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60f4cb39f620b72153b269ad091c2751a6fbdd0a7253aad500d28be34678263a</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-1-killed-4-wounded-after-shooting-near-paris/a-79742256--05dc01bcf479.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-1-killed-4-wounded-after-shooting-near-paris/a-79742256?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French police arrested a suspect after gunshots were fired on the outskirts of Paris in what President Macron described as a racist and terrorist attack.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Sri Lanka: Death of iconic elephant raises habitat concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bde7dabeaa317aaeb8704bdfc5d55affc892c906230c173fa01abc3c3e7b05de</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T09:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-death-of-iconic-elephant-raises-habitat-concerns/a-79735669--6048c81cd2f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-death-of-iconic-elephant-raises-habitat-concerns/a-79735669?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of what was thought to be Sri Lanka’s largest elephant has drawn attention to human-elephant conflict in rural communities. The island country sees a high number of deadly encounters.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Greece joins countries putting age-limits on social media, banning access for kids under 15</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb036e191801295f0eb8b753de7c3cb29d6937523d28f92f652c3bf53e56331a</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T09:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/greece-joins-countries-putting-age-limits-on-social-media-banning-access-for-kids-under-15/a-79739606--e768bcffaa49.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/greece-joins-countries-putting-age-limits-on-social-media-banning-access-for-kids-under-15/a-79739606?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Greece has passed legislation banning social media access for children under 15. New rules will come into effect on January 1, 2027, and are designed to protect children's mental health.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Wadephul says 'threat of famine' due to ongoing wars</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d931f659779b00a5b659759495cc209e4d7b195eb1f826030076d156656727a2</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-wadephul-says-threat-of-famine-due-to-ongoing-wars/live-79738902--60ffe6da3f19.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-wadephul-says-threat-of-famine-due-to-ongoing-wars/live-79738902?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Foreign Minister Johann Wadephul is joining counterparts in Turkey for discussions on a range of interlinked geopolitical crises. Back in Germany, the Bavarian CSU party begins its two-day conference in Munich.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Israel orders home demolitions after soldiers killed in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:010c020bd7102f54fdfebeee850a83a77f91659a43a7fdfc6d9ad6a1d67adaec</id><updated>2026-10-23T20:01:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-orders-home-demolitions-after-soldiers-killed-in-west-bank/a-79739292--2a30f13c2948.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-orders-home-demolitions-after-soldiers-killed-in-west-bank/a-79739292?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Israeli forces will demolish homes in the West Bank after gunmen killed two Israeli soldiers in the West Bank city of Hebron.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea proposes military talks with North again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c91889a4b7ca56f2e06ee422537eae2c283b105650ae1ad97f6c72c940fdafc6</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T07:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-proposes-military-talks-with-north-again/a-79739208--5b2219c381d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-proposes-military-talks-with-north-again/a-79739208?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Korea is attempting to mutually determine the land border with North Korea amid military incidents and escalating tensions.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany sit out FIFA Under-15 World Cup as Russia return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bfcbb5829891b0cc8e6e5c7e967a2a9ba2ec5ee5bbe805d4ef58f38e84291a48</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T07:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-sit-out-fifa-under-15-world-cup-as-russia-return/a-79734040--d1c93bdcd718.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-sit-out-fifa-under-15-world-cup-as-russia-return/a-79734040?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany is one a handful of FIFA's 211 nations to refuse an invitation to play at the inaugural Under-15 World Cup. The tournament will also mark Russia's return to the FIFA fold.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Taiwan braces as El Nino-supercharged Typhoon Champi approaches island</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91fde25d9e8d2c863fe1cbf89b96d001bdfd1666c3163fe1d8f7245f1e73e34c</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T06:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/taiwan-braces-as-el-nino-supercharged-typhoon-champi-approaches-island/a-79738819--5f04cbf55cee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/taiwan-braces-as-el-nino-supercharged-typhoon-champi-approaches-island/a-79738819?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One person has died and thousands have been evacuated as Taiwan prepares for a possible direct hit. Though no longer a "super" typhoon, Champi is still packing winds of nearly 200 kmh and will bring torrential rain.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Musk's Starshield system 'back' in Ukraine, says Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc64a8d52674630369210da28861eb879ea6754ff30d9ce328a0198e3d14572b</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T05:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/musk-s-starshield-system-back-in-ukraine-says-trump/a-79738723--329222d51a85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/musk-s-starshield-system-back-in-ukraine-says-trump/a-79738723?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Trump has said he wouldn't comment on who called for capping Ukraine's Starshield access but added that Elon Musk had "put it back." His account was rejected by Ukraine, which says nothing has changed.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Embarrassing name? How we live with names we don't like</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7832882226a0338807110f34aaa0ae9f6e60e69445c2e54e84585e11cfd4fae5</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T05:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/embarrassing-name-how-we-live-with-names-we-don-t-like/a-79724068--afb6ee0b7720.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/embarrassing-name-how-we-live-with-names-we-don-t-like/a-79724068?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Names are central to our identity, so what happens when that name is a source of ridicule? Research points to negative life outcomes, but some people learn to embrace unfortunate names.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Protesters march to Election Commission demanding CEC Gyanesh Kumar's resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efe8670e295302be14abf210741393f5fb627e35c7061dc0978c98f4ab97b8ad</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T04:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-protesters-march-to-election-commission-demanding-cec-gyanesh-kumar-s-resignation/live-79738437--359ae058742e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-protesters-march-to-election-commission-demanding-cec-gyanesh-kumar-s-resignation/live-79738437?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A coalition of students, farmers and civil society groups has joined calls for Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar's resignation over India's voter roll revision exercise.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
